WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.804 --> 00:00:15.207
reached the field of flowers and uttered a cry of joy.

2
00:00:16.268 --> 00:00:20.871
Peter, who was nearby with the flock of goats, heard her and turned to look.

3
00:00:21.992 --> 00:00:26.156
The whole ground in front of Heidi was filled with gold and yellow blossoms.

4
00:00:27.637 --> 00:00:31.360
Above the gold flowers grew thick bushes of deep blue flowers.

5
00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:35.246
Heidi turned around and ran back to Clara's side.

6
00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:40.608
"Oh, you must come, you must," said Heidi excitedly.

7
00:00:40.628 --> 00:00:44.391
"It is more beautiful than you can imagine."

8
00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.592
"But Heidi, how?"

9
00:00:48.153 --> 00:00:48.853
asked Clara.

10
00:00:48.873 --> 00:00:51.094
"I will help you!"

11
00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:52.195
said Heidi.

12
00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:55.156
"But you are smaller than me.

13
00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:58.658
Oh, if only I could walk!"

14
00:00:59.359 --> 00:00:59.979
said Clara.

15
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.113
Suddenly, Heidi had an idea.

16
00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:07.056
"Peter, Peter, come down here!"

17
00:01:07.656 --> 00:01:08.196
she yelled.

18
00:01:09.678 --> 00:01:12.880
"No, I don't want to," Peter replied.

19
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.582
"I cannot do it alone.

20
00:01:16.002 --> 00:01:17.483
You must come and help me."

21
00:01:17.503 --> 00:01:22.787
"No, I shall do nothing of the kind," said Peter angrily.

22
00:01:24.508 --> 00:01:30.892
Heidi ran up to where Peter sat and said, "If you don't come at once, Peter, I will

23
00:01:30.952 --> 00:01:32.573
do something you won't like!"

24
00:01:33.753 --> 00:01:38.535
Heidi had no idea what she might do, but she was angry at Peter's stubbornness.

25
00:01:40.056 --> 00:01:41.457
Peter was suddenly afraid.

26
00:01:42.557 --> 00:01:49.380
Maybe, just maybe, Heidi knew that he had destroyed Clara's wheelchair and was planning to tell someone.

27
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.902
"If I come, will you promise not to do what you said?"

28
00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:55.463
asked Peter carefully.

29
00:01:55.483 --> 00:02:00.917
"Yes," said Heidi, and so they both went back to Clara.

30
00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:08.339
Heidi told Peter to hold her up on one side, while she took the other, and together they

31
00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:09.659
helped Clara to her feet.

32
00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:15.461
So far, so good, but Clara could not keep upright without support.

33
00:02:15.481 --> 00:02:19.462
"Put your arm around my neck," Heidi told her.

34
00:02:19.482 --> 00:02:22.202
"Peter, give her your arm."

35
00:02:22.763 --> 00:02:29.372
Peter had never done anything like this before, so Heidi showed him how to make a crook with

36
00:02:29.432 --> 00:02:31.393
his arm that Clara could lean on.

37
00:02:32.913 --> 00:02:35.114
Still, they were not very successful.

38
00:02:36.214 --> 00:02:41.316
Peter was taller than Heidi, so Clara was unbalanced and flopped heavily between them.

39
00:02:41.336 --> 00:02:46.517
"Try putting one foot down firmly," Heidi advised her.

40
00:02:48.038 --> 00:02:49.898
Cautiously, Clara tried it.

41
00:02:49.918 --> 00:02:56.020
"That didn't hurt nearly as much as I thought it would," she said.

42
00:02:57.156 --> 00:03:03.720
"Try again," urged Heidi, and Clara placed her other foot, then managed several steps.

43
00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.202
"Oh Heidi," she cried.

44
00:03:07.222 --> 00:03:08.483
"Look at me.

45
00:03:09.143 --> 00:03:09.864
I'm walking!

46
00:03:10.404 --> 00:03:11.165
I'm walking!"

47
00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:18.529
Clara still kept hold of Heidi and Peter, but with each step they could feel her getting steadier

48
00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:19.229
on her feet.

49
00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.052
They didn't have far to go to reach the field of flowers.

50
00:03:24.212 --> 00:03:29.435
When they all sat down among the flowers of gold and blue, Heidi felt so glad at heart

51
00:03:29.815 --> 00:03:31.596
that she wanted to shout for joy.

52
00:03:33.037 --> 00:03:36.319
They were all hungry, since it was long past noon.

53
00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:43.723
They ate their lunch, and soon after they finished, Heidi spotted Grandfather climbing up to get them.

54
00:03:44.804 --> 00:03:50.547
She ran to him to tell him the news about Clara and was so excited that she could

55
00:03:50.627 --> 00:03:51.708
hardly get the words out.

56
00:03:53.372 --> 00:03:56.413
"So you fought the battle and won the day, did you?"

57
00:03:56.893 --> 00:03:59.074
Grandfather said to Clara when he reached her.

58
00:04:00.194 --> 00:04:05.975
He helped her up and made her walk a few steps, putting one arm around her waist and

59
00:04:06.055 --> 00:04:10.337
holding his other arm firmly in front of her so that she could hold on to it.

60
00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:15.658
With this support, she walked with more confidence than before.

61
00:04:16.778 --> 00:04:22.180
Heidi skipped joyfully beside them, and the old man looked as though a great happiness had come to

62
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:25.388
him. "You have worked hard enough for today.

63
00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.873
You can try again tomorrow," he said.

64
00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:34.823
He then lifted her up onto his back, and off they went, down the mountainside.
